    "highlights": "Code syntax highlighting is implemented using `Azeret Mono` at 12px with explicit color spans for tokens (e.g., cyan for `onMessage`, blue for `const`). Additionally, markdown support and variable axis interpolation emphasize specific words natively within text blocks.",
    "insights": [
      "Extensive use of the variable font `PolySans Arabic VF Variable Slim` allows the system to establish hierarchy solely through the `wght` axis (ranging from 400 to 600), while the CSS `font-weight` property remains a constant 300.",
      "`Azeret Mono` is employed exclusively for code blocks and technical metadata at a strict 12px, reinforcing a developer-focused, technical brand identity.",
      "Native system fonts (`-apple-system`) are strategically utilized for micro-UI elements such as user handles and counters, contrasting with the primary custom web fonts to simulate native OS integrations."
